{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And He said, \"Sanctify them today and tomorrow.\"</b> He extended for them time to sanctify: the rest of this day and tomorrow." "<b>The sense of \"and you shall sanctify them.\"</b> That they wash in water, and they indicate this by \"and he shall wash his clothes\" in the manner of \"and if he does not wash and his flesh is not bathed\" (Leviticus 17:16). Therefore Moses said, \"Do not approach a woman\" from now on, so that they be holy and not impure; and whoever approached a woman shall sanctify himself, in the manner of \"and she is sanctified from her impurity\" (II Samuel 11:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:52.771687177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}